    "prompt": "Fill four holes in the procurement skill AND fulfill every round's real market requests. Each round demands one whole case of either tea or cocoa; a case fills the entire cold store. Buying the wrong product loses that service contract irreversibly. Quotes reveal economic terms, not demand. Use the public candidate-world table and any suitable observations to decide what to buy. Choose either supplier; the final cash goal allows one express surcharge in total. Complete 3 rounds with all requests served and cash at least 6848 cents. No particular sensor or observation count is required for scoring. Read /market/contract.json, /skills/procurement.txt and /docs/accounting.txt.",
